{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/34535","id":3282363088,"node_id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs7DpOLQ","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34535","diff_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34535.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34535.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34535","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/34535/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/34535/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/34535/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/statuses/8435c8bc008089ce14bf6a5cfccc2637d4f9371c","number":34535,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Feature][Perf] Support Selective CPU Weight Offloading","user":{"login":"wzhao18","id":51183510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTgzNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51183510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18","html_url":"https://github.com/wzhao18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wzhao18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n## Purpose\nThis PR adds support to selectively offload parameters to CPU based on name matching. One use case is to only offload experts weights for MoE weights, which is useful for low-concurrency settings. This is turned on by passing argument `--cpu-offload-params`\n\n## Test Plan\nTested offloading Kimi K2 NVFP4 on one GB300.\n```\nVLLM_WEIGHT_OFFLOADING_DISABLE_PIN_MEMORY=1 python3 -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n\t--model nvidia/Kimi-K2-Thinking-NVFP4 \\\n\t--trust-remote-code \\\n        --cpu-offload-gb 350 \\\n        --load-format dummy \\\n        --cpu-offload-params w13_weight w2_weight\n```\n\nBenchmarking single-user throughput:\n```\nvllm bench serve \\\n  --backend vllm \\\n  --endpoint /v1/completions \\\n  --num-prompts 5 \\\n  --dataset-name random \\\n  --input-len 100 \\\n  --output-len 100 \\\n  --max-concurrency 1 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --num-warmups 2\n```\n\n## Test Result\n**Before: 15 tok/s**\n```\n============ Serving Benchmark Result ============\nSuccessful requests:                     5         \nFailed requests:                         0         \nMaximum request concurrency:             1         \nBenchmark duration (s):                  32.17     \nTotal input tokens:                      500       \nTotal generated tokens:                  500       \nRequest throughput (req/s):              0.16      \nOutput token throughput (tok/s):         15.54     \nPeak output token throughput (tok/s):    17.00     \nPeak concurrent requests:                2.00      \nTotal token throughput (tok/s):          31.08     \n---------------Time to First Token----------------\nMean TTFT (ms):                          302.71    \nMedian TTFT (ms):                        326.77    \nP99 TTFT (ms):                           327.42    \n-----Time per Output Token (excl. 1st token)------\nMean TPOT (ms):                          61.94     \nMedian TPOT (ms):                        61.93     \nP99 TPOT (ms):                           61.95     \n---------------Inter-token Latency----------------\nMean ITL (ms):                           61.94     \nMedian ITL (ms):                         61.90     \nP99 ITL (ms):                            62.72     \n==================================================\n```\n\n**Offloading MoE weights only: **31 tok/s****\n```\n============ Serving Benchmark Result ============\nSuccessful requests:                     5         \nFailed requests:                         0         \nMaximum request concurrency:             1         \nBenchmark duration (s):                  15.81     \nTotal input tokens:                      500       \nTotal generated tokens:                  500       \nRequest throughput (req/s):              0.32      \nOutput token throughput (tok/s):         31.62     \nPeak output token throughput (tok/s):    34.00     \nPeak concurrent requests:                2.00      \nTotal token throughput (tok/s):          63.24     \n---------------Time to First Token----------------\nMean TTFT (ms):                          244.12    \nMedian TTFT (ms):                        272.78    \nP99 TTFT (ms):                           273.59    \n-----Time per Output Token (excl. 1st token)------\nMean TPOT (ms):                          29.48     \nMedian TPOT (ms):                        29.48     \nP99 TPOT (ms):                           29.49     \n---------------Inter-token Latency----------------\nMean ITL (ms):                           29.48     \nMedian ITL (ms):                         29.47     \nP99 ITL (ms):                            29.85     \n==================================================\n```\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\n- [ ] (Optional) Release notes update. If your change is user facing, please update the release notes draft in the [Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YyVqrgX4gHTtrstbq8oWUImOyPCKSGnJ7xtTpmXzlRs/edit?tab=t.0).\n</details>\n\n","labels":[{"id":7197733874,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABrQSz8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/ready","name":"ready","description":"ONLY add when PR is ready to merge/full CI is needed","color":"ededed","default":false},{"id":8068298936,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAAB4Oh4uA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/v1","name":"v1","description":"","color":"9810B3","default":false},{"id":9543357705,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAACONQVCQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/nvidia","name":"nvidia","description":"","color":"76B900","default":false}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-02-13T19:44:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T03:53:40Z","closed_at":"2026-02-14T04:02:24Z","merged_at":"2026-02-14T04:02:24Z","merge_commit_sha":"b37b679770aade27f33d20c93bf467c6a7fba65d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"heheda12345","id":25218289,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjE4Mjg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25218289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345","html_url":"https://github.com/heheda12345","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heheda12345/repos